      "file": "curl/lib/ftp.c",
      "function": "ftp_statemach_act",
      "line": 2621,
      "code": "case FTP_WAIT220:\n  if(ftpcode == 230)\n    return ftp_state_user_resp(conn, ftpcode, ftpc->state);\n  else if(ftpcode != 220) {\n    failf(data, \"Got a %03d ftp-server response when 220 was expected\",\n          ftpcode);\n    return CURLE_WEIRD_SERVER_REPLY;\n  }",
      "note": "The witness reaches curl's FTP control-state machine. The URL TLV selects the FTP handler and the staged banner TLV `response0` is the 11-byte line `220 Bbzue f2 0a`, so the `FTP_WAIT220` admission checks accept the server banner instead of aborting.",
      "oracle_kind": "gt_parser_checkpoint",
      "kind": "parser_admitted"
    },
    {
      "file": "curl/lib/pingpong.c",
      "function": "Curl_pp_readresp",
      "line": 323,
      "code": "result = Curl_read(conn, sockfd, ptr,\n                   data->set.buffer_size - pp->nread_resp,\n                   &gotbytes);",
      "note": "First curl-side statement that consumes the attacker-controlled FTP reply bytes and materializes them in the pingpong response buffer.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "curl/lib/conncache.c",
      "function": "Curl_conncache_close_all_connections",
      "line": null,
      "code": "char buffer[READBUFFER_MIN];\nconnc->closure_handle->state.buffer = buffer;\nconnc->closure_handle->set.buffer_size = READBUFFER_MIN;\nconn->data = connc->closure_handle;",
      "note": "The one-line fix in `patch.diff` changes only this stack buffer extent to `READBUFFER_MIN + 1`. In the staged vulnerable tree, every ordinary receive buffer still follows the larger contract, for example `preconnect()` allocates `malloc(data->set.buffer_size + 1)` in `curl/lib/multi.c:1539`; the closure handle is the mismatched outlier that makes the 1025-byte cached copy overflow.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "curl/lib/conncache.c",
      "function": "Curl_conncache_close_all_connections",
      "line": 537,
      "code": "char buffer[READBUFFER_MIN];\nconnc->closure_handle->state.buffer = buffer;\nconnc->closure_handle->set.buffer_size = READBUFFER_MIN;\nconn->data = connc->closure_handle;",
      "note": "The one-line fix in `patch.diff` changes only this stack buffer extent to `READBUFFER_MIN + 1`. In the staged vulnerable tree, every ordinary receive buffer still follows the larger contract, for example `preconnect()` allocates `malloc(data->set.buffer_size + 1)` in `curl/lib/multi.c:1539`; the closure handle is the mismatched outlier that makes the 1025-byte cached copy overflow.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "curl/lib/pingpong.c",
      "function": "Curl_pp_readresp",
      "line": null,
      "code": "memcpy(ptr, pp->cache, pp->cache_size);",
      "note": "The saved sanitizer trace reports `AddressSanitizer: stack-buffer-overflow WRITE of size 1025` at this copy, with `Curl_pp_readresp` at `curl/lib/pingpong.c:310:7` as the closest project frame. ASan places the destination in `Curl_conncache_close_all_connections`'s stack object `buffer` at offsets `[32, 1056)`, so a 1025-byte copy starting at the buffer base overruns by one byte into the next stack object.",
      "kind": "sink_function"
    },
